{title: 629 - O Happy Band of Pilgrims}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #629 • VULPIUS • 7.6.7.6.}
{lyricist: Joseph the Hymnographer}
{composer: Melchior Vulpius}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 629}
{meta: tune VULPIUS}
{meta: meter 7.6.7.6.}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D/F#]O happy band [G/D]of [A/E]pilgrims,
[Bm]If onward [G]ye [D/A]will [A]tread
[F#m]With [G]Jesus [D/F#]as [A]your [E7/G#]fellow,
[D/A]To [G]Jesus [Em/B]as [A7/G]your [D/F#]Head!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D/F#]O happy if [G/D]ye [A/E]labor
[Bm]As Jesus [G]did [D/A]for [A]men;
[F#m]O [G]happy [D/F#]if [A]ye [E7/G#]hunger
[D/A]As [G]Jesus [Em/B]hungered [D/F#]then!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D/F#]The trials [A]that [G/D]beset [A]you,
[Bm]The sorrows [G]ye [D/A]endure,
[F#m]The [G]manifold [A]temptations
[D/A]That [G]death [D/A]alone [A7/G]can [D/F#]cure,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D/F#]What are [A]they [D/A]but [G/D]His [A/E]jewels
[Bm]Of right [D]celestial [A]worth?
[F#m]What [G]are [A7/G]they [D/F#]but [A]the [E7/G#]ladder
[D/A]Set up [G]to [D/A]heaven [A7/G]on [D/F#]earth?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D/F#]O happy band [G/D]of [A/E]pilgrims,
[Bm]Look upward [G]to [D/A]the [A]skies,
[F#m]Where [G]such [A7/G]a [D/F#]light [A]affliction
[D/A]Shall [G]win [D/A]you [Em/B]such [A7/G]a [D/F#]prize!
{end_of_verse}
